@startuml 15_sequence_correct_recheck
!include ../style.iuml
title Sequence diagram: what-if, then correct and recheck (a new version)
autonumber
skinparam maxMessageSize 230

actor "Reviewer\n(level 2 or 3)" as RV
participant "Reviewer API\n(/work/claims/{id}/...)" as API
participant "Queue\nservice" as QS
participant "Rule engine" as MR
participant "Intake and\ntriage" as IN
database "Store\n(MongoDB)" as DB
participant "Review log\n(hash chain, signed)" as RL
participant "Security\nlog" as LOG

RV -> API : open a claim from the inbox\n(lease held, identifiers masked)

== Try a correction: nothing is stored ==
RV -> API : POST whatif (proposed changes)\n(permission claims.recheck)
API -> QS : whatif
QS -> MR : evaluate the corrected copy
MR --> QS : 15 results
QS -> LOG : claim_whatif (badge, claim, version,\nnumber of changes)
QS --> RV : each rule before and after

== Correct and recheck ==
RV -> API : POST recheck (changes, reason,\ntick: values checked against the source)
API -> QS : recheck
alt the correction clears a high-severity finding\nand the reviewer lacks claims.decide_high
  QS --> RV : refused
else allowed
  QS -> IN : submit the corrected claim as version n+1
  alt same content as an earlier version
    IN --> QS : nothing new stored
    QS --> RV : refused (no new version)
  else new content
    IN -> MR : evaluate, then triage (lane, score)
    IN -> DB : new document, version n+1, state triaged
    QS -> DB : decision mark_corrected_for_recheck\nfor each cleared finding (only if the lease is valid)
    QS -> RL : review decisions and a recheck_run event\n(links both versions by input hash)
    QS -> LOG : claim_rechecked
    QS -> DB : version n: leased -> decided -> rechecked
    QS --> RV : diff, new lane and score,\nfindings still flagged
  end
end

note over DB
  The original version is never edited. The new version
  goes through the same queue as any claim, and the same
  rules apply to it (two seniors for high severity).
end note
@enduml
